\tag{fdip}
\title{Paired coefficients and a finite connection sum}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A transported cochain operator gives a matrix at each link
configuration. Its determinant can weight a finite sum over
connections, but the paired coefficient producing that determinant
must still make sense when factorials cannot be inverted.
What coefficient survives over the integers or in characteristic
#{2}, and when can its connection sum be normalized?}

